idence that the school monitors whether numeracy capability transfers, and identifies equity gaps."},{"id":"N-C-022","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"TAS","year":"Year 12","title":"Enterprise Computing","ht":"Ms Julie McBride","demand":"Data modelling, spreadsheet formulas and functions, database queries, data visualisation, project costing and scheduling, interpreting performance metrics.","task":"Task 3 Enterprise Project; Trial HSC Examination (T3)","artefact":"Student spreadsheet and database artefacts with formula views; the project brief showing the data-analysis requirement.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Digital numeracy - an area panels rarely see and which strengthens breadth of the claim."},{"id":"N-C-023","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"TAS","year":"Year 12","title":"Food Technology","ht":"Ms Julie McBride","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Recipe scaling and yield conversion, ratio and proportion, nutritional analysis per 100g and per serve, portion and food costing, temperature and time control, sensory evaluation data.","task":"Task 3 Food Product Development - Experimentation and Preparation (T2 Wk7 2026); Task 2 Food Industry Test (T1 Wk7)","artefact":"Product development folios showing scaling, costing and nutritional calculation; sensory evaluation data sheets with student analysis; marked samples across the range.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Everyday and workplace numeracy taught explicitly - maps directly to ACSF Level 3, the HSC minimum standard benchmark."},{"id":"N-C-024","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"TAS","year":"Year 12","title":"Industrial Technology","ht":"Ms Julie McBride","demand":"Measurement and marking out, cutting lists and material optimisation, costing, tolerance, scale drawing, project timelines.","task":"Task 1 Planning; Task 3 Project Development (across T1-T2); Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Management folio pages with cutting lists, costings and timelines; teacher feedback on measurement accuracy; photographs of work where measurement error was identified and corrected.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Feedback explicitly addresses numerical errors until mastery is demonstrated."},{"id":"N-C-025","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"TAS","year":"Year 12","title":"Software Engineering","ht":"Ms Julie McBride","demand":"Algorithm design and efficiency, binary and hexadecimal representation, Boolean logic, data structures, test data design and analysis of results.","task":"Task 3 Software Engineering Project; Trial HSC Examination (T3)","artefact":"Student algorithm and test-data documentation; the explicit teaching sequence for number systems and logic.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Abstract and computational numeracy is explicitly taught, broadening the definition beyond arithmetic."},{"id":"N-C-026","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"TAS","year":"Year 12","title":"Textiles and Design","ht":"Ms Julie McBride","demand":"Pattern scaling and grading, fabric quantity calculation and lay planning, costing, measurement and fit, seam allowance.","task":"Task 1 Major Textiles Project (T4 onward); Trial Examination (T3)","artefact":"Project diary pages showing lay plans, fabric quantity and costing calculations; marked samples.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Spatial and proportional numeracy in a practical course."},{"id":"N-C-027","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Drama","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"Timing and duration of performance pieces, spatial reasoning and blocking, rehearsal scheduling, production budgets in the logbook.","task":"Task 2 Presentation (T1); Group Performance and logbook across the year","artefact":"Logbook extracts showing scheduling and budget planning; rehearsal schedules produced by students.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Numeracy is present in every faculty - closes the 'all subject areas' gap in the SEF Excelling descriptor."},{"id":"N-C-028","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Music 1","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Aural skills: metre and time signature, rhythmic subdivision and proportion, tempo in bpm, interval size, structural proportion. Aural is a discrete examined component.","task":"Aural Skills Examination; Task 2 Solo or ensemble performance evening; Presentation of Electives 2 and 3","artefact":"Aural examination papers with the rhythm and metre questions identified; item analysis of aural results; the explicit teaching sequence for rhythmic subdivision.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"An unexpected but rigorous numeracy evidence source - proportional reasoning assessed formally."},{"id":"N-C-029","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Music 2","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"Time signatures and metric modulation, bar counts and proportional structure in composition, transposition intervals, score durations.","task":"Composition portfolio and Musicology tasks; Aural Examination","artefact":"Annotated student scores showing structural proportion planning; aural task results.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Proportional and structural reasoning evidenced in creative work."},{"id":"N-C-030","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Music Extension","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"Proportional structure across an extended composition portfolio; duration management; statistical or quantitative method within musicology research.","task":"Task 1 Composition portfolio; Task 3 Musicology","artefact":"Portfolio planning documents; musicology research showing quantitative method where used.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Numeracy at the highest achievement levels."},{"id":"N-C-031","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Photography, Video and Digital Imaging","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Exposure as reciprocal and ratio reasoning (f-stops, shutter fractions, ISO), the exposure triangle as a trade-off calculation, aspect ratio, resolution and DPI, print sizing, edit timing.","task":"Task 1 Diary and Portfolio; Task 2 Examination","artefact":"Diary pages showing exposure calculations and reasoning; the explicit teaching resource for the exposure triangle; marked samples.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Explicit teaching of a genuinely difficult numerical concept in a creative subject."},{"id":"N-C-032","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Visual Arts","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"Scale and proportion in the Body of Work, materials quantity and costing, timeline and milestone management, dimensional planning for installation.","task":"Body of Work development across the year; Task 4 Written Examination (Art Criticism and Art History)","artefact":"Visual Arts Process Diary pages showing scale drawings, costings and timelines; marked samples.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Numeracy in project management and spatial reasoning, evidenced in a NESA-marked body of work."},{"id":"N-C-033","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"CAPA","year":"Year 12","title":"Visual Design","ht":"Ms Denise Nicola","demand":"Grid systems and proportion, scale, print and screen dimensions, colour value and tonal ratios, production costing.","task":"Task 1 Design folio; Major Design project","artefact":"Folio pages showing grid construction and dimensional specification; marked samples.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Applied proportional reasoning in design."},{"id":"N-C-034","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Advanced","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Critical numeracy: evaluating quantitative claims, statistics and infographics used persuasively in non-fiction and media texts; managing time and length under examination conditions.","task":"Module C The Craft of Writing; Module B Critical Study; Trial HSC (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Non-fiction and multimodal texts used in class that carry quantitative claims, with the analysis questions attached; marked responses that interrogate a statistic rather than reproduce it.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"","why":"Be honest with the panel: English contributes critical numeracy, not computation. This is a defensible and distinctive claim."},{"id":"N-C-035","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English EAL/D","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Comprehension of numerical information in listening and multimodal texts - dates, quantities, statistics, graphs and infographics - where language and numeracy demands compound.","task":"Listening task; Task 2 Prescribed Text; Module A","artefact":"Listening task transcripts and items containing numerical information, with EAL/D student performance on those items; adjustment records.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Adjustments target a compounded language-and-numeracy demand for an identified equity group."},{"id":"N-C-036","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Extension 1","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Evaluating quantitative evidence within critical and theoretical readings; research scope and sampling of texts.","task":"Task 1 Critical response including related texts; Trial HSC Examination","artefact":"Course reader extracts where critical arguments rest on quantitative claims; student responses evaluating them.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"","why":"Critical numeracy extends to the highest achieving students."},{"id":"N-C-037","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Extension 2","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Major Work project management: word and duration budgets, drafting schedules, milestone planning against the viva voce and submission deadlines.","task":"Task 1 Viva Voce; Task 2 Literature Review; Major Work","artefact":"Major Work journals showing schedule and word-budget planning; the milestone calendar issued to students.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Numeracy as self-management - relevant to Learning culture as well as Curriculum."},{"id":"N-C-038","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Standard","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Interpretation of quantitative stimulus in media and multimodal texts within Texts and Human Experiences and the Common Module; recognising persuasive misuse of data.","task":"Task 1 Common Module; Task 2 Close Study of Text; Module A","artefact":"Multimodal stimulus containing data with the accompanying questions; marked responses.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"","why":"Reaches the largest share of the cohort, including many students in Mathematics Standard."},{"id":"N-C-039","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Studies","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGHEST VALUE IN ENGLISH. Modules use everyday and workplace texts - payslips, timetables, budgets, contracts, workplace documents. This cohort overlaps most heavily with students yet to meet the HSC minimum standard in numeracy.","task":"Task 1 Writing; Task 3 Classwork portfolio; Common Module and elective modules across the year","artefact":"Portfolio evidence of work with payslips, budgets, timetables and workplace documents; cross-referenced list of English Studies students and their HSC minimum standard numeracy status; record of targeted support.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Targeted support for the students furthest from the standard - the strongest equity evidence in the set."},{"id":"N-C-040","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 12","title":"French Beginners","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"Numbers, dates and times, prices and currency, quantities and measures in transactional and informa