5104 grouping system, statistics in authentic texts, dates and durations in spoken texts.","task":"Task 1 Responding to spoken texts; Translation task Japanese to English; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Translation samples where numerical grouping had to be converted; marked responses.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Numeracy accuracy carries assessable consequences in a language course."},{"id":"N-C-044","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Advanced","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"COMPARISON ANCHOR. Calculus, functions, statistical analysis - underpins Physics, Chemistry, Engineering Studies and Economics.","task":"Task 1 Test (T4); Task 2 Test (T1); Task 3 Test (T2); Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Cross-referenced student-level comparison of Mathematics Advanced rank against performance on numerate items in Physics, Chemistry and Economics.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Shows the school analyses whether numeracy capability transfers between subjects - a sophisticated data-analysis claim."},{"id":"N-C-045","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Extension 1","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"COMPARISON ANCHOR. Source of faculty expertise for whole-school numeracy professional learning.","task":"Task 1 Test (T4); Task 2 Test (T1); Task 3 Test (T2); Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Records of Mathematics staff delivering or co-designing professional learning for other faculties; co-marking or moderation records.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"","why":"The school identifies expertise within its staff and draws on it to develop the professional learning community."},{"id":"N-C-046","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Extension 2","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"COMPARISON ANCHOR. Highest level of mathematical reasoning in the school; a source of peer tutoring and mentoring capacity.","task":"Task 1 Test (T4); Task 2 Test (T1); Task 3 Test (T2); Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Any peer tutoring or student-led numeracy support program records, with participation and outcome data.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"","why":"Student agency in the numeracy strategy - often the missing piece in evidence sets."},{"id":"N-C-047","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Standard 1","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"COMPARISON ANCHOR. Financial mathematics, measurement, statistics and networks - the course whose cohort most overlaps with students yet to meet the HSC minimum standard in numeracy.","task":"Task 1 Test (T4); Task 2 Test (T1); Task 3 Assignment (T2)","artefact":"Course results mapped against HSC minimum standard numeracy attainment for the same students; the faculty's list of students requiring targeted support and what was provided.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Establishes the baseline the whole-school strategy is trying to move. Include Maths so the tracker shows triangulation, not separation."},{"id":"N-C-048","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Standard 2","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"COMPARISON ANCHOR. Statistical analysis including bivariate data and normal distribution, financial mathematics, networks - skills directly reused in Business Studies, Geography, PDHPE and Science.","task":"Task 1 Test (T4); Task 2 Test (T1); Task 3 Test (T2); Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"A mapping document produced with other faculties showing where Standard 2 topics are assumed or reused in their courses, and when each is taught relative to the other course's task.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"","why":"Sequencing alignment across faculties is concrete, checkable evidence of a whole-school approach."},{"id":"N-C-049","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Business Services VET (BSB30120 Certificate III in Business)","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Training package units require processing financial transactions, producing spreadsheets, business document numeracy and data entry accuracy. ACSF numeracy levels are specified in the training package.","task":"Competency-based assessment across units; optional HSC examination","artefact":"Mapping of the qualification's ACSF numeracy levels against the HSC minimum standard (also ACSF Level 3); competency evidence portfolios showing numeracy tasks; assessor records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"An externally benchmarked numeracy standard the school already meets - strong, independent corroboration."},{"id":"N-C-050","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Entertainment Industry Specialisation VET","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"Extension of the above: production scheduling, detailed budgeting, technical specification and measurement.","task":"Competency-based assessment across specialisation units","artefact":"Production paperwork produced by students - schedules, budgets, technical specifications.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Progression in numeracy demand across a VET pathway."},{"id":"N-C-051","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Entertainment Industry VET","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Rigging load and safe working load calculation, electrical power (watts, amps, phase loading), measurement and rigging plots, cue timing, budgets. Numeracy errors here are safety-critical.","task":"Competency-based assessment; mandatory work placement (70 hours); optional HSC examination","artefact":"Competency evidence for load and power calculation units; work placement supervisor feedback referencing numeracy; risk assessments produced by students.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Numeracy with real consequence, verified by an external workplace - highly credible to a panel."},{"id":"N-C-052","goal":"N","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Hospitality Cookery VET","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Recipe conversion and yield, portion control, food cost percentage and menu costing, stock rotation and ordering quantities, temperature and time control, unit conversion.","task":"Competency-based assessment; mandatory work placement (70 hours); optional HSC examination","artefact":"Costed recipe cards and yield calculations produced by students; work placement records referencing measurement and costing; assessor observation records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Everyday and workplace numeracy at ACSF Level 3, assessed against national industry standards."},{"id":"N-W-01","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"HSC minimum standard numeracy - cohort attainment and time series","ht":"Deputy Principal / Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"From NESA Schools Online: proportion of each Year 12 cohort who have met the numeracy standard, number of attempts required, and the not-yet-met list tracked through the year. Present as a 3-year trend, disaggregated by equity group.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 1 (baseline), updated each test window","why":"The only external, standardised numeracy measure available to a Stage 6 school. Without a time series this element is very hard to argue."},{"id":"N-W-02","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"HSC RAP item analysis - numerate items across all courses","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning with all Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"In Scout / RAP, identify questions in every HSC course with a quantitative demand (calculation, graph or table interpretation, proportional reasoning) and compare school mean against state. Build a single cross-faculty table.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 1 (post-HSC release), reviewed Term 3","why":"This is the strongest single artefact you can produce. It converts 'we all teach numeracy' from an assertion into a measured, cross-curricular claim - and it is only possible because you are a Stage 6 school."},{"id":"N-W-03","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Incoming Year 11 numeracy profile from feeder campuses","ht":"Deputy Principal / Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Year 9 NAPLAN numeracy and Check-in Assessment numeracy data for incoming students from Sydney Secondary College Balmain and Leichhardt campuses, plus other feeder schools. Establishes the starting point.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 4 (enrolment) and Term 1","why":"A Stage 6 school cannot claim growth without a credible entry baseline. This also evidences the Y10-Y11 transition theme explicitly named in SEF V3."},{"id":"N-W-04","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Assessment schedule numeracy audit","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Using Appendix 8 Scope and Sequence and each course's assessment schedule, map every Year 11 and 12 task that carries a numeracy demand by term. Shows density, spread and any term where numerate tasks cluster or vanish.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 1","why":"Demonstrates the school-wide approach is planned and monitored, not the sum of individual teachers' goodwill."},{"id":"N-W-05","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Assessment task notification and marking criteria audit","ht":"Head Teachers, moderated by Deputy Principal","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Sample tasks from every faculty and check whether numeracy demands are named in the task description, the outcomes, and the marking criteria. Record the proportion that do, then re-audit after intervention.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 1 baseline, Term 4 re-audit","why":"A before-and-after proportion is a genuine improvement measure, and it is entirely within the school's control."},{"id":"N-W-06","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Faculty teaching and learning programs annotated for numeracy","ht":"All Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Programs showing where numeracy is explicitly taught, by whom and when - not merely where it appears. Include the adjustment history.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 2","why":"Panels distinguish sharply between a program that mentions numeracy and one that shows it was planned, taught and revised."},{"id":"N-W-07","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Cross-faculty numeracy sequencing map","ht":"Head Teacher Mathematics with all Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"A one-page map produced jointly by Mathematics and other faculties showing when a skill is first taught in Mathematics relative to when it is assumed in Science, HSIE, PDHPE, TAS and VET tasks - and what was resequenced as a result.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 2","why":"Concrete, checkable and unusual. Directly evidences teachers collaborating across faculties to share curriculum knowledge."},{"id":"N-W-08","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Professional learning records - numeracy across the curriculum","ht":"Deputy Principal / PL Coordinator","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"PL plans, session materials, attendance, and - critically - the evaluation of impact on practice. Include Mathematics staff delivering PL to other faculties.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Ongoing; collate Term 3","why":"The SEF Delivering descriptor for Literacy and numeracy focus is specifically about PL that builds teacher knowledge of effective numeracy strategies through the curriculum."},{"id":"N-W-09","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"PDP goals referencing numeracy (APST 2.5)","ht":"Principal / Deputy Principals","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"De-identified count and sample of Performance and Development Plan goals addressing numeracy strategies in the teacher's own subject area, with evidence of progress.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Term 1 (goal setting) and Term 3 (review)","why":"Shows a coordinated whole-school approach to developing professional practice rather than isolated interest."},{"id":"N-W-10","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Classroom observation and instructional rounds with a numeracy look-for","ht":"Head Teachers / Deputy Principals","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Observation notes using an agreed numeracy look-for (e.g. does the teacher make the numerical demand explicit; are worked examples used; is numerical error addressed to mastery). Include the feedback given.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 2 and 3","why":"Observation evidence of practice is what separates Sustaining and Growing from Delivering. Documentation alone will not carry it."},{"id":"N-W-11","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Moderation and consistent teacher judgement of numerate task components","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Records of cross-faculty co-marking of the numeracy components of tasks - e.g. Geography tools, Physics data analysis, Business Studies finance - with the agreed standard and any recalibration.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 2 and 3","why":"Directly evidences processes supporting teachers' consistent, evidence-informed judgement and moderation."},{"id":"N-W-12","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Student work sample bank across all faculties","ht":"All Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Three annotated samples per course (high / middle / low achievement) showing the numeracy demand, the student response and the teacher feedback. Aim for coverage of every faculty.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"Term 3","why":"The SEF Excelling descriptor requires reaching students 'across all achievement levels and subject areas'. A bank organised by achievement level answers that phrase directly."},{"id":"N-W-13","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Equity group tracking","ht":"Head Teacher Learning Support / Deputy Principal","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Numeracy attainment and progress disaggregated for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, EAL/D students, students with disability and adjustments, and low-SES students. Include what was done differently.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 2 and Term 4","why":"SEF V3 explicitly requires progress of equity groups to be equivalent to that of all students. Aggregate-only data will be challenged."},{"id":"N-W-14","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Tell Them From Me and student focus groups on numeracy","ht":"Head Teacher Wellbeing / Year Advisers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Student voice on confidence with numerical demands in their subjects, where they get stuck, and whether they see numeracy as relevant beyond Mathematics. Run focus groups by faculty.","etype":"Student / staff voice","due":"Term 2","why":"Triangulates quantitative evidence with student voice, which panels look for. Also evidences student agency."},{"id":"N-W-15","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Staff survey on confidence teaching numeracy in their subject","ht":"Deputy Principal / PL Coordinator","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Short pre/post survey of all teaching staff on confidence and on whether they have identified the numeracy demands in their own courses. Repeat after PL.","etype":"Student / staff voice","due":"Term 1 and Term 4","why":"A simple before-and-after that demonstrates evaluation of PL impact, which the SEF requires."},{"id":"N-W-16","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Executive and faculty meeting minutes","ht":"Principal / Executive","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Minutes showing numeracy as a standing agenda item, the data discussed, and decisions made. Extract the specific items rather than submitting whole minutes.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Ongoing; extract Term 3","why":"Evidences distributed leadership and shared responsibility for the strategy over time."},{"id":"N-W-17","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"School Excellence Plan progress monitoring and evaluative statements","ht":"Principal / SEP team","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"The numeracy initiative in the SEP, its improvement measures, progress monitoring entries and the annual reflection - showing what changed as a result of evaluation.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Ongoing; Term 4 reflection","why":"Ties every other artefact back to the plan. Without it the evidence set reads as a collection rather than a strategy."},{"id":"N-W-18","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Parent and carer communication about numeracy","ht":"Principal / Deputy Principals","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Newsletter items, information evenings, minimum standard letters, and the guidance given to parents about supporting numeracy in their child's subjects.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 1 and 3","why":"The SEF V3 Excelling descriptor for Literacy and numeracy focus explicitly requires parents/carers to be supported as collaborative partners. This is the most commonly missing piece of an otherwise strong evidence set."},{"id":"N-W-19","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Careers, work placement and post-school transition evidence","ht":"Careers Adviser / VET Coordinator","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Employer and supervisor feedback from VET work placement referencing numeracy performance; numeracy requirements of the courses and jobs students are applying for.","etype":"Student / staff voice","due":"Terms 2 and 3","why":"External, third-party verification of student numeracy in an authentic setting - rare and persuasive."},{"id":"N-W-20","goal":"N","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Targeted intervention records for students not yet meeting the standard","ht":"Head Teacher Learning Support / Deputy Principal","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Named (de-identified for submission) list of students yet to meet the HSC minimum standard in numeracy, the support provided, attempts made, and outcomes.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Each test window","why":"Demonstrates the strategy reaches the students furthest from the standard, with measurable outcomes."},{"id":"R-C-001","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Aboriginal Studies","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"Reading community-authored sources, government and policy texts and academic writing; managing sources with sharply different registers and authority.","task":"Task 1 Research Report (T1 Wk8); Task 2 Multi-Modal Presentation (T2 Wk10)","artefact":"Reading list with complexity noted; student annotations of a dense policy source; three marked samples across the range.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"Term 2, Week 4","why":"Disciplinary reading established in the Preliminary year rather than assumed on entry."},{"id":"R-C-002","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Aboriginal Studies","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"Reading dense policy, legal and government texts, community-authored sources and academic writing on Aboriginal experience; distinguishing perspective and voice across sources with very different registers.","task":"Task 1 Research Report (T4 Wk7 2025); Task 3 Major Project (T2 Wk8 2026)","artefact":"The reading list for the Major Project with text complexity noted; annotated student notes showing how a dense source was unpacked; three marked samples across the achievement range.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Disciplinary reading is taught, not assumed - including reading across sharply different registers."},{"id":"R-C-003","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Ancient History","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Task 1 is a Source Analysis Test on Thera - close reading of translated and fragmentary primary sources under examination conditions in Term 1.","task":"Task 1 Source Analysis Test - Thera (T1 Wk9, in hall); Task 2 Historical Investigation Essay (T2 Wk7)","artefact":"The Thera source booklet with reading demand annotated; item analysis separating comprehension errors from content errors; the source-unpacking scaffold.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"A Term 1 Year 11 reading diagnostic under examination conditions - the earliest hard reading data the school can generate outside English."},{"id":"R-C-004","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Ancient History","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Sustained close reading of translated primary sources, fragmentary and archaeological evidence, and competing scholarly interpretations. Provenance, reliability and usefulness are reading judgements.","task":"Task 1 Source-based task; Trial HSC Examination (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Source booklets with the reading demand annotated (register, archaism, translation effects); the scaffold used to teach source unpacking; marked responses showing inferential and evaluative reading.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Inferential and evaluative reading assessed formally within a mandated syllabus skill."},{"id":"R-C-005","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Business Studies","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"Task 1 requires reading and analysing business media; reading case studies and stimulus material for argument and evidence.","task":"Task 1 Media Report and Analysis - Nature of Business (T1 Wk8); Task 2 Stimulus Based Task (T2 Wk9)","artefact":"The media texts with reading demand mapped; marked analyses showing accurate reading rather than summary.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Media reading taught and assessed early in Stage 6."},{"id":"R-C-006","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Business Studies","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"Reading annual reports, case studies, business media and financial commentary; extracting argument from stimulus under time pressure. Stimulus-based skills is a 20% component.","task":"Task 2 Marketing case study research task (T1 Wk7); Task 3 Finance (T2 Wk6)","artefact":"The case study texts with their reading demand mapped; item analysis of stimulus comprehension questions; marked responses showing accurate reading of the stimulus.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Comprehension isolated as a measurable component within a content subject."},{"id":"R-C-007","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Economics","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Task 1 is a Stimulus Based Task in Term 1 Week 8. Stimulus-based skills is a 25% component in Year 11 - higher than Year 12.","task":"Task 1 Stimulus Based Task (T1 Wk8, in class); Task 2 Research Report - in class extended response (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Item analysis separating stimulus comprehension from content knowledge; the economic vocabulary sequence taught; marked responses.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"The weighting is highest in Year 11, so this is the best point to diagnose and act on reading of economic stimulus."},{"id":"R-C-008","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Economics","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading economic commentary, policy statements and multimodal stimulus combining prose, tables and graphs; high nominalisation and abstraction. Stimulus-based skills 20%.","task":"Task 2 Topic Test - multiple choice and short answer stimulus (T1 Wk7); Task 3 Stimulus-based in-class extended response (T2 Wk7)","artefact":"Item analysis separating stimulus comprehension errors from content knowledge errors; the vocabulary list taught explicitly; marked responses.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Separates 'could not read it' from 'did not know it' - the most useful reading diagnostic available in a content subject."},{"id":"R-C-009","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Geography","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"Reading maps, imagery, climate data and case study reports and integrating them; geographical inquiry requires reading across text types.","task":"Task 1 Topic Test - Earth's Natural Systems and Geographical Tools (T1 Wk9); Task 2 Research Task - Geographical Investigation (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Stimulus sets showing the range of text types; marked responses showing synthesis across them.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Non-continuous and multimodal reading, from the Preliminary year."},{"id":"R-C-010","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Geography","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"Reading synoptic and multimodal texts - maps, satellite imagery, climate graphs, case study reports - and integrating them into a single interpretation. Non-continuous text reading is a distinct skill.","task":"Task 1 Research Task - Ecosystems and Global Biodiversity (T4 Wk8 2025); Task 4 Trial HSC (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Stimulus sets showing the range of text types students must integrate; marked responses demonstrating synthesis across text types.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Reading of non-continuous and multimodal text - a demand that a whole-school reading focus often overlooks."},{"id":"R-C-011","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"History Extension","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"HIGHEST VALUE FOR CRITICAL READING. Reading historiography - dense academic prose, competing theoretical positions, and the reading of one historian against another.","task":"Task 1 Source-based task; Task 2 History Project","artefact":"Course reader extracts with complexity noted; student annotations of a historiographical text; the History Project bibliography showing reading breadth and depth.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Sustained academic reading at the top of the achievement range - the ceiling of the school's reading demand."},{"id":"R-C-012","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Legal Studies","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"Reading legislation, cases and scenario material; Task 1 scenario analysis requires reading a fact pattern accurately before any legal reasoning.","task":"Task 1 Research Task / Short Answer / Scenario Analysis - Basic Legal Concepts (T1 Wk7); Task 2 Study Guide / Extended Response (T2 Wk9)","artefact":"Scenario texts with the reading routine taught; marked responses where misreading of the scenario is distinguishable from misapplication of law.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"A clean separation of reading failure from content failure, in Term 1 of Year 11."},{"id":"R-C-013","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Legal Studies","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"Reading legislation, case law, treaties, media reporting and law reform commission material; statutory language and legal register are a distinct reading challenge.","task":"Task 2 Essay; Trial HSC Examination (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Extracts of legislation and case law with the explicit reading scaffold used; student notes showing legal register decoded; marked responses.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Explicit strategies for a register students meet nowhere else in the school."},{"id":"R-C-014","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Modern History","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Task 1 Source Analysis on The Cuban Revolution - close reading of primary sources, propaganda and historiography under timed conditions.","task":"Task 1 Source Analysis Task - The Cuban Revolution (T1 Wk7); Task 2 Research Essay / Historical Investigation (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"The source booklet with reading demand annotated; item analysis of source comprehension items; three marked samples.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Comparable to the Year 12 source task - one half of a genuine two-year reading comparison."},{"id":"R-C-015","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Modern History","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading primary sources in translation, propaganda, statistical sources and historiography; corroborating and contesting sources against each other.","task":"Task 1 Source-based task; Trial HSC Examination (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Source booklets with reading demand annotated; item analysis of source comprehension questions separated from content questions; marked responses at three achievement levels.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Reading comprehension isolable and measurable within an HSC course, twice a year."},{"id":"R-C-016","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Society and Culture","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"Reading ethnographic, sociological and media texts; reading research material for the Task 1 research task and judging credibility.","task":"Task 1 Research Task - Social and Cultural World (T1 Wk7); Task 2 Focus Group Essay (T2 Wk7)","artefact":"Research task bibliographies and student notes; the source-appraisal scaffold that later underpins the PIP.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"The reading base the Year 12 Personal Interest Project depends on."},{"id":"R-C-017","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Society and Culture","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"Reading ethnographic, sociological and media texts; reading research literature for the Personal Interest Project, including judging source credibility.","task":"Task 1 PIP Proposal (T4 Wk7 2025); Task 3 Research Essay (T2 Wk5 2026)","artefact":"PIP literature review sections showing reading breadth and critical judgement; the source-evaluation scaffold taught.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Independent academic reading evidenced in a NESA-marked major work."},{"id":"R-C-018","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 11","title":"Studies of Religion II","ht":"Mr Robert Bury","demand":"Reading sacred texts in translation and scholarly commentary; archaic register and unfamiliar cultural reference are the barriers.","task":"Task 1 Research Task - Religion of Ancient Origin (T1 Wk8); Task 2 In Class Essay (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Sacred text extracts with the reading scaffold used; student annotations.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Explicit teaching of a high-archaism register from the Preliminary year."},{"id":"R-C-019","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"HSIE","year":"Year 12","title":"Studies of Religion II","ht":"Mr Rob Bury","demand":"Reading sacred texts in translation, exegetical and doctrinal writing, and scholarly commentary; register and archaism are significant barriers.","task":"Task 1 Religious Tradition Depth Study; Task 3 Religion in Australia post-1945 (T2)","artefact":"Sacred text extracts with the reading scaffold used; student annotations showing exegetical reading.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Explicit teaching of a high-archaism register."},{"id":"R-C-020","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Science","year":"Year 11","title":"Biology","ht":"Mr Dean Dimarti","demand":"Reading scientific procedures and secondary sources; Tier 3 vocabulary load is heaviest in the transition from Stage 5 to Stage 6.","task":"Task 1 Skills task based on excursion data (T1 Wk10); Task 2 Depth Study Scientific Report, enzyme activity (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Procedure and secondary source texts with vocabulary demand mapped; the explicit vocabulary sequence taught in Term 1.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Targets the Stage 5 to Stage 6 vocabulary jump, which is where reading in Science most often breaks down."},{"id":"R-C-021","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Science","year":"Year 12","title":"Biology","ht":"Ms Traci Lewis","demand":"Reading scientific reports, secondary source data and technical procedures; decoding Tier 3 vocabulary and nominalised process language. Working Scientifically 60%.","task":"Task 2 Skills task, Module 6 Genetic Change (T1 Wk7); Task 3 Depth Study - analysis of a first-hand investigation (T2 Wk7)","artefact":"Secondary source texts used in the depth study with vocabulary demand mapped; student annotations; marked responses showing accurate reading of method and results.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Technical reading taught explicitly rather than assumed from Stage 5."},{"id":"R-C-022","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Science","year":"Year 11","title":"Chemistry","ht":"Mr Dean Dimarti","demand":"Reading technical procedures, symbolic representation and problem stems; moving between prose, symbol and diagram.","task":"Task 1 Depth Study - Scientific Report (T1 Wk8); Task 2 Skills Task, Module 2 (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Item analysis of questions where misreading the stem caused the error; the stem-unpacking routine taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Reading identified as a cause of error inside a science result."},{"id":"R-C-023","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Science","year":"Year 12","title":"Chemistry","ht":"Ms Traci Lewis","demand":"Reading technical procedures, safety data, symbolic representation and scientific argument; moving between prose, symbolic and diagrammatic representations of the same idea.","task":"Task 2 Skills task (T1 Wk7