T VALUE. Sustained close reading of complex literary texts, including Shakespeare, poetry and prose fiction, plus critical readings in the Critical Study module. Reading is the core business.","task":"Module B Critical Study of Text; Module A Textual Conversations; Trial HSC (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Annotated texts showing close reading; marked responses evidencing inferential and evaluative reading; the school's close reading protocol.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"The anchor of the reading claim - but on its own it proves only that English teaches reading."},{"id":"R-C-066","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 11","title":"English EAL/D","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGHEST VALUE FOR EQUITY. Task 1 studies a range of fiction texts, Task 2 a range of non-fiction. Reading with a compounding language load - idiom, cultural reference, register.","task":"Task 1 Reading to Write: Transition to Senior English - Imaginative Task with Reflection (T1 Wk8); Task 2 Texts and Society - Presentation including Listening (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Reading progression phase data for EAL/D students; adjustment records; annotated texts showing scaffolding; marked responses.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"The clearest place in the school where reading growth can be tracked against a published progression."},{"id":"R-C-067","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English EAL/D","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGHEST VALUE FOR EQUITY. Reading with a compounding language load: idiom, cultural reference, register and implicit meaning. Reading progressions are directly applicable.","task":"Task 2 Prescribed Text; Module A; Listening and reading tasks","artefact":"Reading progression data for EAL/D students (phases); adjustment records; annotated texts showing scaffolding; marked responses.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"The clearest place in the school where reading growth can be tracked against a progression."},{"id":"R-C-068","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 11","title":"English Extension 1","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Reading theoretical and critical texts alongside primary texts in Text, Culture and Values; reading one position against another.","task":"Task 1 Imaginative response / reflection (T1 Wk10); Task 2 Presentation, TED Talk style (T3 Wk2)","artefact":"Course reader with complexity noted; student annotations of theoretical texts.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Theoretical reading at the ceiling of the Preliminary demand."},{"id":"R-C-069","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Extension 1","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Reading literary theory and criticism alongside primary texts; reading one critical position against another.","task":"Task 1 Critical response including related texts; Trial HSC Examination","artefact":"Course reader with complexity noted; student annotations of theoretical texts.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Theoretical reading at the ceiling of the school's demand."},{"id":"R-C-070","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Extension 2","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"Independent wide reading for the Major Work, plus the Literature Review requiring sustained reading of a self-selected field.","task":"Task 2 Literature Review; Task 1 Viva Voce; Major Work","artefact":"Literature reviews showing reading breadth and depth; reading journals from the Major Work process.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Self-directed reading - evidence of reading as an established disposition, not a taught compliance."},{"id":"R-C-071","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 11","title":"English Standard","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading to Write: Transition to English Standard is explicitly a transition module - the school's designed on-ramp into Stage 6 reading for the largest cohort.","task":"Task 1 Reading to Write: Transition to English Standard - Writing Task under timed conditions (T1 Wk8); Task 2 Contemporary Possibilities (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"The transition module program showing what reading support is built in; annotated texts across three achievement levels; marked responses.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"","why":"A named, designed transition into Stage 6 reading - directly evidences the transition theme as well as the reading claim."},{"id":"R-C-072","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Standard","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Close reading of prescribed texts and related material for the largest share of the cohort; the module structure builds from guided to independent reading.","task":"Task 2 Close Study of Text; Module A; Trial HSC (T3 Wks 4-5)","artefact":"Annotated texts across three achievement levels; the close reading protocol; marked responses showing inferential reading.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Reaches the largest share of the cohort, including most students at risk on the minimum standard."},{"id":"R-C-073","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 11","title":"English Studies","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGHEST VALUE FOR THE AT-RISK COHORT. Elective K 'Achieving Through English' and Elective G 'Part of the Family' use everyday, workplace and public information texts. This cohort overlaps most with students yet to meet the minimum standard in reading.","task":"Task 1 Reading to Write Creative Response (T1 Wk10); Task 2 Elective K Achieving Through English - Critical Response (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Portfolio evidence of functional reading; a cross-referenced list of English Studies students and their HSC minimum standard reading status; targeted support and re-sit records.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Targeted support for the students furthest from the standard, identified in Year 11 rather than Year 12."},{"id":"R-C-074","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"English","year":"Year 12","title":"English Studies","ht":"Ms Stephanie Ward","demand":"HIGHEST VALUE FOR THE AT-RISK COHORT. Everyday and workplace reading - instructions, contracts, workplace documents, public information texts. This cohort overlaps most heavily with students yet to meet the HSC minimum standard in reading.","task":"Task 1 Writing; Task 3 Classwork portfolio; Common Module and elective modules","artefact":"Portfolio evidence of functional reading tasks; a cross-referenced list of English Studies students and their HSC minimum standard reading status; record of targeted support and re-sit outcomes.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Targeted support for the students furthest from the standard - the strongest equity evidence in the set."},{"id":"R-C-075","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 11","title":"Chinese Continuers","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"YEAR 11 ONLY. Reading Chinese characters - a logographic script with no phonetic decoding route. Task 2 requires responding to Chinese texts.","task":"Task 1 Responding to spoken Chinese texts and interview (T1 Wk7); Task 2 Response to Chinese texts and Writing Task (T2 Wk7)","artefact":"Character recognition and reading fluency records; reading items with error analysis; the character-learning sequence taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Decoding in its purest form, with no phonetic shortcut - a striking illustration of reading taught outside English."},{"id":"R-C-076","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 11","title":"French Beginners","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"Reading authentic and adapted French texts; Task 1 requires responding in English and French to written texts. Cognates, false friends and reading for gist versus detail.","task":"Task 1 Response in English and French to written texts (T2 Wk3); Task 3 Final Examination (T3 Wks 9-10)","artefact":"Reading items with error analysis distinguishing decoding from comprehension failure; the reading strategy sequence taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Reading strategies taught explicitly and their effect measured."},{"id":"R-C-077","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 12","title":"French Beginners","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"Reading authentic and adapted French texts - notices, correspondence, articles - decoding cognates and false friends, and reading for gist as well as detail.","task":"Reading and responding task; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Reading items with error analysis distinguishing decoding from comprehension failure; the reading strategy sequence taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Reading strategies taught explicitly and their effect measured - unusually clean data."},{"id":"R-C-078","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 11","title":"Italian Beginners","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"Reading authentic and adapted Italian texts; Task 1 requires responding in English and Italian to written texts.","task":"Task 1 Response in English and Italian to written texts (T2 Wk3); Task 3 Final Examination (T3 Wks 9-10)","artefact":"Reading items with error analysis; the reading strategy sequence taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Second-language reading makes strategy use visible."},{"id":"R-C-079","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 12","title":"Italian Beginners","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"Reading authentic and adapted Italian texts, decoding cognates, and reading for gist and detail.","task":"Reading and responding task; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Reading items with error analysis; the reading strategy sequence taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Second-language reading makes strategy use visible in a way first-language reading rarely does."},{"id":"R-C-080","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 12","title":"Japanese Beginners","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading three scripts - hiragana, katakana and kanji - in combination. Decoding is explicit, effortful and directly observable.","task":"Reading texts task; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Script recognition and reading fluency records; reading items with error analysis by script.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Decoding made visible. A memorable illustration that reading is taught outside English."},{"id":"R-C-081","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 11","title":"Japanese Continuers","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Task 2 is explicitly a reading task requiring responses in English and/or Japanese, across hiragana, katakana and kanji; inferring unknown kanji from context and radicals.","task":"Task 2 Reading task requiring responses in English and/or Japanese (T2 Wk7, 5 June); Task 1 Prepared oral and in class writing (T1 Wk9)","artefact":"Reading task with error analysis by script; evidence of inference-from-context strategies taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"A named reading task with isolable error data, in a language faculty."},{"id":"R-C-082","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Languages","year":"Year 12","title":"Japanese Continuers","ht":"Ms Cher Ellis","demand":"Reading extended authentic Japanese texts across three scripts; inferring meaning of unknown kanji from context and radicals.","task":"Task 2 Reading task; Translation Japanese to English; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Reading and translation samples showing inference from context; error analysis.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Inference from context taught and assessed explicitly."},{"id":"R-C-083","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 11","title":"Mathematics Advanced","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Reading multi-clause problem stems and mathematical prose; interpreting notation as text.","task":"Task 1 Written Task (T1 Wk7); Task 2 Written Task (T2 Wk7)","artefact":"Item analysis on long-stem questions; the stem-unpacking routine taught in Mathematics.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Reading identified as a variable inside a Mathematics result, from Term 1 of Year 11."},{"id":"R-C-084","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Advanced","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Reading multi-clause problem stems and mathematical prose; interpreting notation as text.","task":"Task 1-3 Tests; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Item analysis on long-stem questions; the stem-unpacking routine taught.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Reading identified as a variable inside a Mathematics result."},{"id":"R-C-085","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 11","title":"Mathematics Extension 1","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Reading formal proof and compressed mathematical argument.","task":"Task 1 Written Task (T1 Wk9); Task 2 Written Task (T2 Wk8)","artefact":"Student annotations of a worked proof; evidence of how proof reading is taught; Mathematics staff contribution to whole-school reading PL.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"","why":"Mathematics as a contributor to the whole-school reading strategy, not an exception to it."},{"id":"R-C-086","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Extension 1","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Reading proof and formal mathematical argument - a dense, highly compressed register.","task":"Task 1-3 Tests; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Student annotations of a worked proof; evidence of how proof reading is taught.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"","why":"Reading a compressed formal register, taught explicitly."},{"id":"R-C-087","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Extension 2","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Reading extended proof and unfamiliar problem framings; the highest reading compression in the school.","task":"Task 1-3 Tests; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Student annotations of unfamiliar problems; any peer tutoring records where reading of problems was the focus.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"","why":"Reading at the highest level of compression - and a source of peer support capacity."},{"id":"R-C-088","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 11","title":"Mathematics Standard","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS AND THE CRITICAL COHORT. Worded problems and contextual scenarios carry a heavy reading load. This cohort overlaps most with students yet to meet the minimum standard in reading.","task":"Task 1 Written Task (T1 Wk7); Task 2 Written Task (T2 Wk9)","artefact":"Item analysis distinguishing reading errors from mathematical errors on worded questions; cross-referenced list of Mathematics Standard students and their HSC minimum standard reading status.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Where reading failure and mathematical failure are most often confused - and most consequential."},{"id":"R-C-089","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Standard 1","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Reading worded problems, contextual scenarios, tables and infographics; identifying what is being asked. Reading failure is a common cause of mathematical failure in this cohort.","task":"Task 3 Assignment (T2); Task 1 and 2 Tests","artefact":"Item analysis distinguishing reading errors from mathematical errors on worded questions; the question-unpacking routine taught in Mathematics.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"Include Mathematics so the tracker shows reading is everyone's business - and because worded problems are where reading and numeracy meet."},{"id":"R-C-090","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"Mathematics","year":"Year 12","title":"Mathematics Standard 2","ht":"Ms Ronie Quinn","demand":"READING IN MATHEMATICS. Extended worded problems with multimodal stimulus - tables, networks, scenarios. Reading load in HSC Standard 2 papers is substantial.","task":"Task 1-3 Tests; Trial HSC (T3)","artefact":"Item analysis on the longest-stem questions; comparison of performance on short-stem versus long-stem items of equivalent mathematical difficulty.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"","why":"A precise, defensible measure of reading load effects, generated from data the faculty already has."},{"id":"R-C-091","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 11","title":"Business Services VET (BSB30120 Certificate III in Business)","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. BSBINS302 Organise workplace information and BSBWHS311 require reading policies, procedures and workplace documents. ACSF reading levels are specified in the training package.","task":"Task 1 Let's Get Tech Savvy (T1 Wk10); Task 2 Organising Business Safety (T2 Wk8); Task 3 Working in Industry (T3 Wk5)","artefact":"Mapping of the qualification's ACSF reading levels against the HSC minimum standard (also ACSF Level 3); competency portfolios showing document reading; assessor records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"An externally benchmarked reading standard the school already meets."},{"id":"R-C-092","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Business Services VET (BSB30120 Certificate III in Business)","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading workplace documents, policies and procedures, and business correspondence. ACSF reading levels are specified in the training package.","task":"Competency-based assessment across units; optional HSC examination","artefact":"Mapping of the qualification's ACSF reading levels against the HSC minimum standard (also ACSF Level 3); competency portfolios showing document reading; assessor records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"An externally benchmarked reading standard the school already meets."},{"id":"R-C-093","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Entertainment Industry Specialisation VET","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"Reading production paperwork, technical riders and detailed specifications at greater independence.","task":"Competency-based assessment across specialisation units","artefact":"Production paperwork read and acted on by students; assessor observation records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Progression in reading independence across a VET pathway."},{"id":"R-C-094","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Entertainment Industry VET","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading safety documentation, technical specifications, rigging plots, run sheets and cue sheets. Misreading has safety consequences.","task":"Competency-based assessment; mandatory work placement (70 hours)","artefact":"Competency evidence for documentation units; work placement supervisor feedback referencing reading of instructions; student-produced run sheets.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Reading with real consequence, verified by an external workplace."},{"id":"R-C-095","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 11","title":"Entertainment Industry VET (Statement of Attainment towards CUA30425)","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. White Card and work health and safety units require reading safety documentation accurately before work placement. Also technical specifications, run sheets and rigging plots.","task":"Task 1 White Card (T1 Wk4, prior to work placement); Task 3 Safe and Sound (T2 Wk6); Task 4 Bump in the Light (T3 Wk7)","artefact":"Competency evidence for safety documentation units; work placement supervisor feedback on reading of instructions; student-produced risk assessments and run sheets.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Reading with safety consequence, verified externally - and it happens in Term 1 of Year 11."},{"id":"R-C-096","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 12","title":"Hospitality Cookery VET","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. Reading recipes and standard recipe cards, food safety procedures, allergen and labelling information, and dockets under time pressure.","task":"Competency-based assessment; mandatory work placement (70 hours)","artefact":"Competency evidence showing procedural reading; work placement records; assessor observation of reading accuracy under service conditions.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Functional reading at ACSF Level 3 assessed against national industry standards."},{"id":"R-C-097","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 11","title":"Hospitality Cookery VET (SIT20421 Certificate II in Cookery)","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"HIGH VALUE. SITXFSA005/006 require reading food safety procedures and allergen information accurately; recipes and dockets are procedural reading under time pressure.","task":"Task 1 Safety in the Kitchen (T2 Wk2); Task 2 Service Please (T2 Wk10)","artefact":"Competency evidence showing procedural reading; assessor observation of reading accuracy under service conditions; work placement records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Functional reading with consequence, assessed against national industry standards."},{"id":"R-C-098","goal":"R","kind":"course","team":"VET","year":"Year 11","title":"Hospitality Food and Beverages VET (SIT20322 Certificate II in Hospitality)","ht":"Ms Denise Haire","demand":"YEAR 11 ONLY. Reading menus, dockets, beverage specifications and service procedures accurately and quickly.","task":"Task 1 Safety in the Kitchen (T2 Wk2); Task 2 Service Please (T2 Wk10)","artefact":"Competency evidence showing accurate reading of orders and specifications; assessor observation notes; work placement records.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"","why":"Reading accuracy under time pressure in a real service setting."},{"id":"R-W-01","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"HSC minimum standard READING attainment and time series","ht":"Deputy Principal / Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"From NESA Schools Online: proportion of each cohort who have met the reading standard, attempts required, and the not-yet-met list tracked from first attempt in Year 10 or 11. Present as a 3-year trend, disaggregated by equity group.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 1 baseline, updated each test window","why":"Your only external standardised reading measure. Repeatable, so it can carry a genuine growth claim for students below the standard."},{"id":"R-W-02","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"HSC RAP item analysis - comprehension and stimulus items across all courses","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning with all Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"In Scout / RAP, identify questions in every HSC course that require comprehension of supplied text - source analysis, stimulus, case study, problem stems - and compare school mean against state. Build one cross-faculty table.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 1 (post-HSC release), reviewed Term 3","why":"The strongest single artefact for the whole-school half of the claim. Only a Stage 6 school can produce this breadth. Label it cohort improvement, not student growth."},{"id":"R-W-03","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Year 11 entry reading baseline","ht":"Deputy Principal / Careers Adviser","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Year 9 NAPLAN reading and Check-in Assessment reading data for incoming Year 11 students from the Balmain and Leichhardt campuses and other feeder schools, held against the Stage 6 courses each student selected.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 4 (enrolment) and Term 1","why":"Without this there is no interval and therefore no growth claim. Also evidences the Y10-Y11 transition theme named in SEF V3."},{"id":"R-W-04","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Comparable-task progression analysis, Year 11 to Year 12","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning with faculty HTs","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"For the pairs on the 'Stage 6 progression' sheet, compare the same cohort's performance on the reading component twelve months apart. Start with the Modern History and Ancient History source tasks.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 1 and Term 3","why":"Internal growth data over a defined interval, generated from assessments the school already runs. The most efficient answer to the growth claim."},{"id":"R-W-05","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Shared reading rubric and moderation records","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"A common rubric for literal, inferential and evaluative reading, applied to source and stimulus responses across faculties, with cross-faculty co-marking records and any recalibration.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 2 and 3","why":"Evidences consistent, evidence-informed teacher judgement AND the whole-school claim in a single artefact."},{"id":"R-W-06","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Text complexity audit across Stage 6 courses","ht":"Head Teacher Teaching and Learning","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"For each course, sample what students are actually required to read - length, lexical density, nominalisation, technical vocabulary load - and compare Year 11 against Year 12. Shows whether reading demand escalates deliberately.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 2","why":"Directly evidences longitudinal monitoring of learning pathways. Unusual, and it demonstrates the school understands what it is asking of readers."},{"id":"R-W-07","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Glossary of Key Words - consistent teaching of NESA directive verbs","ht":"All Head Teachers, coordinated by DP","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Both handbooks carry the Glossary as an appendix (Year 12 Appendix 6, Year 11 Appendix 8). Gather evidence that it is explicitly taught in every faculty: teaching resources, student work showing the verb decoded, and item analysis where misreading the verb caused the error.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Term 1","why":"A school-wide reading artefact you already publish. Evidence that it is taught rather than merely printed is cheap and directly supports the whole-school claim."},{"id":"R-W-08","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Assessment task notification readability audit","ht":"Head Teachers, moderated by Deputy Principal","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Sample task notifications from every faculty and assess whether students can read the task itself - sentence length, unglossed technical terms, layout, directive verbs. Record the proportion meeting an agreed standard, act, then re-audit.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 1 baseline, Term 4 re-audit","why":"A before-and-after proportion is a genuine improvement measure entirely within the school's control - and if students cannot read the task, nothing else matters."},{"id":"R-W-09","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Faculty teaching and learning programs annotated for reading","ht":"All Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Programs showing where reading is explicitly taught - vocabulary, comprehension strategy, text structure, critical reading - by whom and when, with the revision history.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Term 2","why":"Panels distinguish sharply between a program that lists texts and one that shows how students were taught to read them."},{"id":"R-W-10","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Explicit vocabulary instruction records","ht":"All Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Faculty-level Tier 2 academic and Tier 3 technical word lists, the teaching sequence used, and any pre/post vocabulary assessment. Science and HSIE at the Stage 5-6 transition are the highest-value places to start.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 1 and 3","why":"Vocabulary is the most tractable component of reading to teach and measure, and pre/post data on it is a legitimate growth measure."},{"id":"R-W-11","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Item analysis separating comprehension error from content error","ht":"Faculty Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"For source and stimulus tasks in Ancient History, Modern History, Legal Studies, Economics, Business Studies, Geography, Physics and Chemistry, analyse whether errors arose from misreading the supplied text or from not knowing the content.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Terms 1 and 2","why":"The most useful reading diagnostic available outside English, and it costs nothing new to run. Also the clearest evidence that reading is treated as everyone's business."},{"id":"R-W-12","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Reading strategy professional learning and its evaluation","ht":"Deputy Principal / PL Coordinator","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"PL plans, session materials, attendance, and the evaluation of impact on classroom practice. Include English staff delivering PL to other faculties.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Ongoing; collate Term 3","why":"The SEF Delivering descriptor for Literacy and numeracy focus is specifically about PL that builds teacher knowledge of effective strategies through the curriculum."},{"id":"R-W-13","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Classroom observation with a reading look-for","ht":"Head Teachers / Deputy Principals","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Observation notes using an agreed reading look-for: is the reading demand made explicit; is a comprehension strategy modelled; is vocabulary pre-taught; are students reading, or being read to.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 2 and 3","why":"Observation evidence is what separates Sustaining and Growing from Delivering. Documentation alone will not carry it."},{"id":"R-W-14","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Annotated text bank across all faculties and achievement levels","ht":"All Head Teachers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Three annotated texts per course (high / middle / low achievement) showing the reading demand, how the student worked through it, and the teacher feedback on their reading.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"Term 3","why":"The Excelling descriptor requires reaching students across all achievement levels and subject areas. A bank organised by achievement level answers that phrase directly."},{"id":"R-W-15","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"EAL/D reading progression data and adjustment records","ht":"Head Teacher EAL/D or Learning Support","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Reading phase judgements against the EAL/D Learning Progression, moderated, with the adjustments made for each student.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Each semester","why":"The only published reading progression available to you, applied to an identified equity group. It measures reading growth directly."},{"id":"R-W-16","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Targeted reading intervention records","ht":"Head Teacher Learning Support / Deputy Principal","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"De-identified list of students yet to meet the HSC minimum standard in reading, the support provided, attempts made, and outcomes - beginning in Year 11, not Year 12.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Each test window","why":"Demonstrates the focus reaches the students furthest from the standard, with measurable outcomes."},{"id":"R-W-17","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Disability provisions and access arrangements for reading","ht":"Head Teacher Learning Support","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Records of reader provisions, assistive technology, accessible text formats and extra time granted for reading-related need, and how these are used in school assessment as well as the HSC.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 1 and 3","why":"Evidences that 'all students' includes students for whom reading access is the barrier - a group often absent from reading evidence sets."},{"id":"R-W-18","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Equity group disaggregation","ht":"Head Teacher Learning Support / Deputy Principal","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Reading attainment and progress disaggregated for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, EAL/D students, students with disability and low-SES students, with what was done differently.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 2 and Term 4","why":"SEF V3 explicitly requires progress of equity groups to be equivalent to that of all students. Aggregate-only data will be challenged."},{"id":"R-W-19","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Evidence for strong readers","ht":"Head Teachers English, HSIE, Science","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Extension course reading - History Extension historiography, English Extension 1 and 2, Science Extension journal literature - showing challenge and growth at the top of the range.","etype":"Student work sample","due":"Term 2","why":"The goal says ALL students. An evidence set built only around at-risk readers demonstrates intervention, not a whole-school focus. This row exists to stop that."},{"id":"R-W-20","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Library and wide reading engagement data","ht":"Teacher Librarian","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Borrowing data, wide reading programs, reading culture initiatives, and any student reading records.","etype":"Data / student performance","due":"Term 3","why":"Evidences reading culture. Present it under Learning culture, not Student growth - engagement is not achievement and a panel will say so."},{"id":"R-W-21","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Tell Them From Me and student focus groups on reading","ht":"Head Teacher Wellbeing / Year Advisers","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Student voice on the reading load in their subjects, where they get stuck, and whether they see themselves as readers. Run focus groups by faculty.","etype":"Student / staff voice","due":"Term 2","why":"Triangulates quantitative evidence with student voice. Also evidences student agency."},{"id":"R-W-22","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Staff survey on confidence teaching reading in their subject","ht":"Deputy Principal / PL Coordinator","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Short pre/post survey of all teaching staff on confidence, and on whether they have identified the reading demands of their own courses.","etype":"Student / staff voice","due":"Term 1 and Term 4","why":"A simple before-and-after demonstrating evaluation of PL impact, which the SEF requires."},{"id":"R-W-23","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"PDP goals referencing reading (APST 2.5)","ht":"Principal / Deputy Principals","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"De-identified count and sample of Performance and Development Plan goals addressing reading strategies in the teacher's own subject area.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Term 1 and Term 3","why":"Shows a coordinated whole-school approach to developing practice rather than isolated interest."},{"id":"R-W-24","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Executive and faculty meeting minutes","ht":"Principal / Executive","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Minutes showing reading as a standing agenda item, the data discussed, and the decisions made. Extract the specific items rather than submitting whole minutes.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Ongoing; extract Term 3","why":"Evidences distributed leadership and shared responsibility over time."},{"id":"R-W-25","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"School Excellence Plan progress monitoring and evaluative statements","ht":"Principal / SEP team","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"The reading initiative in the SEP, its improvement measures, progress monitoring entries and annual reflection, showing what changed as a result of evaluation.","etype":"Program & planning document","due":"Ongoing; Term 4 reflection","why":"Ties every other artefact back to the plan. Without it the evidence set reads as a collection rather than a strategy."},{"id":"R-W-26","goal":"R","kind":"whole","team":"Whole school","year":"","title":"Parent and carer communication about reading","ht":"Principal / Deputy Principals","demand":"","task":"","artefact":"Newsletter items, information evenings, minimum standard letters, and guidance to parents on supporting reading in senior subjects.","etype":"Practice & observation","due":"Terms 1 and 3","why":"The SEF Excelling descriptor for Literacy and numeracy focus explicitly requires parents/carers to be supported as collaborative partners. Most commonly the missing piece."}];
